CONTRACT FOR DIVERSION RELATED SERVICES
between
THE LARAMIE COUNTY COMMUNITY JUVENILE SERVICES JOINT POWERS
BOARD
And
THE CITY OF CHEYENNE, OFFICE OF YOUTH ALTERNATIVES
This Contract for Diversion Related Services (hereinafter “Agreement) is made and entered
into by and between the Laramie County Community Juvenile Services Joint Powers Board, 310
W. 19th Street, Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001 (“BOARD”) and the City of Cheyenne, Youth
Alternatives, 1328 Talbot Court, Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001 (“CONTRACTOR”).  The parties
agree as follows:
I.
PURPOSE
The purpose of this Agreement is to provide funding to CONTRACTOR to facilitate hiring
and utilizing a Juvenile Diversion Coordinator (“COORDINATOR”) position. This position is
intended to work directly with the Laramie County District Attorney’s Office to reduce truancy
rates and identify behavioral concerns by implementing effective interventions for youth
struggling with attendance and behavioral issues in Laramie County.  These are services that could
otherwise be rendered directly by the BOARD for the benefit of the public.  This Agreement does
not constitute a grant.  It is a contract to purchase services provided by COORDINATOR as
described in Attachment A, which is incorporated into this contract.
II.
TERM AND FUNDING
This Agreement shall commence on January 1, 2025 or on the date this Agreement is fully
executed by the duly authorized representatives of the parties to this Agreement, whichever is later.
This Agreement shall remain in effect through June 30, 2026.  This Agreement may be renewed
subject to the mutual agreement of the parties, in writing, as to term, scope and cost of services,
and availability of funding.  This Agreement may be terminated in accordance with the terms and
conditions set forth herein.
The source of funding for the BOARD to enter into this Agreement and to make payments
for services to CONTRACTOR thereunder is funding which the BOARD receives from Laramie
County, Wyoming, a governmental entity.  As this Agreement is contingent upon the receipt of
said funding, then in the event that the BOARD does not receive any or all funding from Laramie
County necessary to fund or make payments under this Agreement, then BOARD may terminate
this Agreement consistent with the terms of Section V, paragraph D of this Agreement.
III.
PAYMENT
Through the approval of this Agreement, the BOARD has approved possible payment of
up to $156,251.30 (One Hundred and Fifty-Six Thousand, Two Hundred Fifty-One Dollars and
1:26 pm, Dec 12 2024
