IV.
RESPONSIBILITIES OF CONTRACTOR
A.
CONTRACTOR shall hire and manage the Juvenile Diversion Coordinator
(“COORDINATOR”) position to work cooperatively with the CONTRACTOR and Laramie
County District Attorney’s Office.  This position will follow the Diversion Procedures set
forth by the Laramie County District Attorney’s Office.  This position’s responsibilities will
relate to the provision of the services which are described in Attachment A and include the job
duties set forth in Attachment A.
B.
CONTRACTOR shall provide with their monthly invoices a report of the number
of juveniles served during the month and cumulatively by the CONTRACTOR’s services provided
pursuant to this Agreement.
C.
CONTRACTOR shall provide a report within seven days of the conclusion of each
month which will include a narrative description of significant issues and opportunities, the
number of youths served by these services and the total number of contact hours provided by each
program during the previous month.  CONTRACTOR shall provide all other reports as may be
required by BOARD regarding the nature of the services being provided or other aspects of the
CONTRACTOR’S performance under this Agreement.
D.
CONTRACTOR shall collect and submit juvenile justice data in accordance with
Wyo. Stat. §7-19-503.
